{"title":"So Many Different Mes","link":"https://kottke.org/26/10/so-many-different-mes","date":1791922080000,"content":"\n         \t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886550-1e0a1bfe.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886550-1e0a1bfe.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886550-1e0a1bfe.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>Japanese photographer and artist <a href=\"https://tomokosawada.com\">Tomoko Sawada</a> works primarily in self-portraiture. For her first project, she visited ID photo booths to take hundreds of photos of herself, dressed, posed, and presented differently. <a href=\"https://www.tokyoweekender.com/art_and_culture/tomoko-sawada-photographer-interview\">Eugenie Shin of Tokyo Weekender calls</a> that 1998 project, <a href=\"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/94742\">ID 400</a>, “a dizzying grid of strangers who are all actually the same woman”.</p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886001-c3624924.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886001-c3624924.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886001-c3624924.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>For subsequent projects, Sawada says she’s continued to “examine the relationship between outer appearance and inner self through different concepts”.</p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886440-afb730c1.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886440-afb730c1.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1791886440-afb730c1.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>(via <a href=\"https://www.tokyoweekender.com/art_and_culture/tomoko-sawada-photographer-interview\">tokyo weekender</a>)\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Tomoko%20Sawada\">Tomoko Sawada</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"f4eaa147d11571c195b60c4f0f651f49e8be57f06136c060f62cf07c2bd83464","category":"Sites"}